# man page for lensyxe.
# Rendered into a roff file at package time by `go run ./internal/...`-free
# tooling; this is the source.
#
# Written by hand rather than generated. A man page generator is a dependency, and
# the page for a tool with eleven subcommands is a page, not a book.

.TH LENSYXE 1 "2026" "lensyxe" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lensyxe \- score the engineering health of a repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lensyxe
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lensyxe
analyzes a source tree and reports an Engineering Health Score from code
complexity, dependency hygiene, and git history. Every figure is computed locally;
the only outbound request the tool can make is the optional
.B \-\-explain
layer, and it is off unless configured.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B analyze
Score a repository. The main entry point.
.TP
.B status
The same analysis in a few lines. Does not record a run to the history database.
.TP
.B setup
Propose a
.I .lensyxe.yml
derived from a measurement of this repository. Nothing is written without
.BR \-\-write .
With
.B \-\-headless
it takes every default and never prompts, for servers and containers.
.TP
.B installer
Add or remove shell, PATH, and application integration.
.TP
.B blast
Files that historically changed in the same commit as the ones being changed.
.TP
.B cognitive
A 0-100 friction index from variable lifetime, call density, and scope depth.
.TP
.B decay
Files that stopped changing, single-author silos, and activity half-life.
.TP
.B topology
Recency-weighted bus factor, hidden co-change coupling, boundary violations.
.TP
.B gap
Static complexity against real runtime execution, from a pprof, OTel export, or
access log.
.TP
.B diff
Compare engineering health between two commits.
.B log
is an alias.
.TP
.B history
The recorded health timeline.
.B log
is an alias.
.TP
.B watch
Re-analyze on every change.
.TP
.B serve
The local dashboard and JSON API.
.B ui
is an alias.
.TP
.B version
Build metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config
Path to a Lensyxe configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean.
.TP
.B 1
A finding prevented completion.
.TP
.B 2
A configured threshold was breached.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .lensyxe.yml
Per-repository configuration. Every key is optional; see
.IR docs/CONFIGURATION.md .
.TP
.I ~/.config/lensyxe/history.db
The local health history. SQLite, on this machine only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LENSYXE_AI_KEY
Holds the key for the optional explanation layer. Lensyxe never reads it unless
explanation is requested.
.TP
.B LENSYXE_AI_PROVIDER
.BR openrouter ", " openai ", or " gemini .
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation:
.UR https://github.com/zelvior/lensyxe
.UE
